<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "https://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- cctrans-cli is a byte-for-byte copy of the main CCTrans binary, bundled
       inside the Tauri helper (CCTransTauri.app) and fork-exec'd by it for
       translation / benchmarks / login-item changes.

       Why this exists: the Tauri helper (cctrans-tauri) is itself sandboxed. A
       sandboxed process MUST NOT fork-exec another binary that initializes its
       OWN App Sandbox container — the child traps in _libsecinit_appsandbox at
       launch (EXC_BREAKPOINT / SIGTRAP), before main(). That is exactly the
       crash Apple hit on 0.3.2 (Guideline 2.1 App Completeness).

       com.apple.security.inherit makes this copy run INSIDE the parent's
       sandbox instead of creating its own, so libsecinit does not re-init a
       container. An inherited helper therefore MUST NOT declare its own
       application-groups, application-identifier, or network entitlements — it
       receives all of them (App Group + Keychain group + network.client) from
       cctrans-tauri.
       build-mas.zsh deliberately does not append identifier keys to this file. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.inherit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
